fcitx5-slm-ime (1.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Security: only the user's own engine may use the conversion server. The
    server writes a new random token at every start to
    $XDG_DATA_HOME/slm-ime/server-token (mode 0600) and refuses requests without
    it, so that other accounts on the machine and web pages in a browser can no
    longer read conversions or write into the history. Restart fcitx5 (or log in
    again) after the upgrade: an engine of 1.1.0 does not send the token.
  * Security: the history is readable by the user only (0600, directory 0700);
    nothing is learned or kept in password and sensitive fields; the take-back
    (Ctrl+Shift+Insert) is forgotten when the focus moves or the cursor is moved
    after a commit.
  * Key bindings: a key binding profile (Default, MS-IME, ATOK) and the keys of
    every operation for the Custom profile, in fcitx5-configtool.
  * F6 to F10 put the active phrasal unit (the whole reading while typing) in
    hiragana, katakana, half-width katakana, full-width letters and letters.

 -- Osamu Ogasawara <osamu.ogasawara@gmail.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0900

fcitx5-slm-ime (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * The model is trained on FineWeb-2 (Japanese web pages) besides the Japanese
    Wikipedia: the character error rate on web text falls from 7.25 % to 4.89 %.
  * The candidates from Anthy are put in order by the model, after the text before
    the phrasal unit, and are fetched in the background.
  * The last characters of a long conversion are no longer cut off.
  * Without the text before the cursor from the application, the engine sends the
    text committed before; Ctrl+Shift+Insert takes the last commit back.

 -- Osamu Ogasawara <osamu.ogasawara@gmail.com>  Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0900

